{% set local_problem %}
<p>Priceville's rapid growth has brought hundreds of new homes to the area — many with builder-grade gutter systems that meet minimum code but struggle with real-world storms. These sectional gutters have seams every 10 feet, and each seam is a potential failure point. During heavy rainfall, they overflow and send water toward your foundation instead of away from it.</p>

<p>Established Priceville homes face different challenges. Properties along the river roads and in older neighborhoods have gutters that have weathered decades of Alabama weather. Seams have separated, hangers have loosened, and the cumulative effects of humidity and temperature swings have taken their toll.</p>

<p>Morgan County's red clay soil makes these problems worse. Unlike sandy soil that absorbs water, clay forces runoff to pool and spread. When gutters overflow, that water doesn't disappear — it accumulates around your foundation. Over time, this leads to cracks, settling, and basement moisture.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters eliminate the seam problem entirely. Custom-fabricated on-site to fit your home exactly, they have no weak points to fail. For Priceville homes — whether brand new or well-established — seamless gutters provide the reliable protection our weather demands.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters (made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>Why does this matter? Because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint in a sectional gutter system is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that can separate over time. Seamless gutters eliminate these problems entirely.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Priceville home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline — not generic sections forced to fit.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We're not a distant company that occasionally serves Priceville — we're your actual neighbors. Our mailing address in Hartselle is just 8 miles down the road, and we've been serving Morgan County for over 20 years.</p>

<p>That proximity means something. When you call for an estimate, we can often be there the same day. When you schedule installation, there's no long wait while trucks travel from Huntsville or Birmingham. And if you ever need follow-up service, we're minutes away. That's the advantage of working with a truly local company.</p>
